src/staking/AbstractStakingStrategy.sol:_redeemShares:100|class=C15|High|After a partial liquidation tokenizes a withdraw request via _postLiquidation, _redeemShares computes the escrowed amount to burn as w.yieldTokenAmount * sharesToRedeem / w.sharesAmount from the base WithdrawRequest while discarding the TokenizedWithdrawRequest split it just created, so an unprivileged liquidated account redeeming first over-claims the shared escrowed sUSDe/USDe and leaves the liquidator (or remaining depositors) short, with no clamp on sharesToRedeem and no global conservation backstop to revert it.|src/staking/AbstractStakingStrategy.sol
